{"answer":"The scoring freeze starts when a team reaches one point below the game-winning score. From that point, that team can score the game-winning point only while serving.

Example: in a game to 25, a team freezes at 24. That team cannot win the final point unless it is serving. The other team may continue normal rally scoring until it also reaches its freeze point.

For win-by-two games: if the score becomes tied at or beyond the initial freeze point, both teams become unfrozen and normal rally scoring resumes. After that, a team freezes again whenever its next point would win the game by two. If the score ties again, both teams unfreeze again. This continues until one team wins by two, and the game-winning point must always be scored while serving.","conflict":false}
